{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3336","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3336","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3336\",\"parent_revision\":\"c946cecc81e32e396302c2674799c4a221732b8f\",\"root_revision\":\"5d6450b0fd59001dadc9cc76f54ede5e88190b4ba408bdb82972ac8b49189641\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe root cause behind #3329's deletion, generalized: `skills/backlog/SKILL.md` re-explained MCP tool parameters and return shapes in hand-written prose that the tool's own docstring/`Field(description=...)` annotations already stated \u2014 and that duplicate was structurally guaranteed to drift, because FastMCP regenerates the live tool schema from the code every server start, while a prose copy in a skill file changes only when someone remembers to edit it. That mechanism is what produced the deleted skill's \\\"12 tools\\\" heading against 28 real ones, a dead storage-format claim, and a broken `fastmcp` invocation example.\\n\\nConfirmed during #3329 this isn't unique to that one skill: `plugins/development-harness/README.md`'s \\\"Core backlog tools\\\" table has the identical shape (filed separately as #3335).\\n\\nGoal: audit other `dh:*` skills for the same pattern \u2014 prose that restates an MCP tool's parameters, return fields, or behavior, checkable live against the tool's actual schema via `ToolSearch`. Where found: delete the restatement from the skill, and if a genuine content gap exists, add it to the tool's own docstring instead (verified in #3329 to be the correct destination \u2014 it's literally the schema the agent is shown when deciding how to call the tool, a stronger and self-maintaining hook that a skill-file restatement can never be).\\n\\nUser-provided context: see #3329 for the full investigation this generalizes from, including three concrete examples where this exact check (comparing a doc's claim against the live `ToolSearch` schema) revealed the doc was either already redundant or actively wrong.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T09:48:18.754462Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: chore: Audit other dh:* skills for hand-written MCP tool documentation that duplicates and drifts from live tool schemas\\nDate: 2026-08-30\\nGoal: Find and fix (or file) other dh:* skills that restate MCP tool parameters/return shapes in prose that drifts from the live ToolSearch schema, the same mechanism that caused #3329's \\\"12 tools vs 28\\\" defect.\\nConditions:\\n1. Current inventory of dh:* skill directories under plugins/development-harness/skills/ (post-#3329 deletion count) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Which of those skills (SKILL.md + bundled references/agents files) contain prose naming or describing an MCP tool's parameters, return fields, or behavior | Status: DERIVABLE\\n3. For each candidate hit, whether the live tool schema (via ToolSearch) already states the same thing verbatim/equivalently (REDUNDANT), contradicts it (STALE), or omits it (GAP) | Status: DERIVABLE\\n4. Whether any confirmed GAP is small enough to relocate into the tool's own docstring inline during this task, versus large enough to warrant its own follow-up item | Status: DERIVABLE\\n5. Whether #3335 (README table) or #3329 (deleted dh:backlog skill) overlap with any candidate found here (they should be excluded, already tracked/closed) | Status: AVAILABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 2\\nDERIVABLE count: 3\\nMISSING count: 0\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Follow-up from #3329 (dh:backlog dead-skill cleanup)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f6b4f8b07c9e5d3be2c139335ff02ddac6dc5bef5217802b21685463ebbd6724\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABReqhUA\"}"}